1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,185
There. Beautiful.

2
00:01:02,265 --> 00:01:03,785
Thank you.

3
00:01:03,865 --> 00:01:05,344
Are you two really being lovebirds,

4
00:01:05,424 --> 00:01:07,345
or is this just an act?

5
00:01:07,425 --> 00:01:09,505
We agreed to stay married.

6
00:01:10,865 --> 00:01:13,745
Get all those trees out of here.
I don't like them.

7
00:01:13,825 --> 00:01:15,985
Neen, Neen!

8
00:01:16,065 --> 00:01:18,265
Please listen to me!

9
00:01:18,345 --> 00:01:20,905
Stop bullshitting me! Stop it!

10
00:01:20,985 --> 00:01:22,905
-Stop it!
-Neen, that's enough!

11
00:01:23,505 --> 00:01:25,985
Then you can stay with her all you want.

12
00:01:26,065 --> 00:01:27,785
No matter how hard it is,

13
00:01:27,865 --> 00:01:29,945
I won't let go of her hand.

14
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:41,985
You're together almost all the time,

15
00:01:42,065 --> 00:01:44,185
yet she still found a way to surprise you.

16
00:01:44,265 --> 00:01:45,545
Ms. Runch is awesome.

17
00:01:48,225 --> 00:01:49,385
She was here?

18
00:01:49,465 --> 00:01:51,025
Yes. She just left.

19
00:01:51,105 --> 00:01:53,145
Wait, you didn't see each other?

20
00:02:04,385 --> 00:02:05,425
Runch!

21
00:02:08,345 --> 00:02:09,584
Neen.

22
00:02:12,145 --> 00:02:14,065
I was just stopping by quietly.

23
00:02:14,145 --> 00:02:15,665
You didn't have to come out here.

24
00:02:16,265 --> 00:02:17,625
Take your flowers.

25
00:02:23,385 --> 00:02:26,305
You think a bouquet of flowers
can fix everything?

26
00:02:38,985 --> 00:02:40,065
Yes, Mom?

27
00:02:40,825 --> 00:02:42,225
I'm not at the office yet.

28
00:02:42,305 --> 00:02:44,225
I'll call you when I get there.

29
00:02:44,305 --> 00:02:45,345
Bye.

30
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:11,545
Second attempt.

31
00:03:18,545 --> 00:03:20,065
What can I get you?

32
00:03:20,145 --> 00:03:22,305
I'd like these three, please.

33
00:03:22,385 --> 00:03:23,385
Sure.

34
00:03:25,065 --> 00:03:27,345
Can I earn M points here?

35
00:03:27,425 --> 00:03:29,745
Yes. You may scan your receipt
on the M Card app

36
00:03:29,825 --> 00:03:31,625
to earn M points.

37
00:03:32,225 --> 00:03:34,225
-Can I scan to pay?
-Sure.

38
00:03:37,665 --> 00:03:39,265
Dessert, from Ms. Runch.

39
00:03:40,225 --> 00:03:41,945
They're all yours, Ms. Nat.

40
00:03:42,025 --> 00:03:43,625
Flowers, from Ms. Runch.

41
00:03:47,465 --> 00:03:49,065
Please get them out of here.

42
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,985
-Chocolate, from--
-I know.

43
00:03:51,065 --> 00:03:52,745
Please get that out of here.

44
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:05,625
MOM

45
00:04:16,665 --> 00:04:17,585
For this matter,

46
00:04:17,665 --> 00:04:19,944
I'd like to change our whole plan.

47
00:04:21,745 --> 00:04:23,425
Please turn over to page…

48
00:04:26,505 --> 00:04:29,025
Excuse me, Ms. Runch. Your mother called.

49
00:04:33,105 --> 00:04:34,545
Please excuse me.

50
00:04:43,945 --> 00:04:46,145
Yes, Mom? Is something wrong?

51
00:04:46,225 --> 00:04:47,865
<i>Nothing, honey.</i>

52
00:04:47,945 --> 00:04:49,305
<i>I'm perfectly fine.</i>

53
00:04:49,385 --> 00:04:51,985
<i>I was just wondering</i>
<i>if you've had lunch yet.</i>

54
00:04:54,545 --> 00:04:56,785
Mom, I'm in a meeting.

55
00:04:56,865 --> 00:04:58,145
<i>I'm sorry, honey.</i>

56
00:04:58,225 --> 00:05:00,025
<i>I really didn't know.</i>

57
00:05:14,825 --> 00:05:17,065
MOM

58
00:05:21,825 --> 00:05:23,145
Yes, Mom?

59
00:05:23,225 --> 00:05:25,185
<i>Have you left the office yet, Runch?</i>

60
00:05:26,225 --> 00:05:28,745
Not yet, Mom. I'm still finishing my work.

61
00:05:28,825 --> 00:05:31,905
Did you eat yet?
Do you want me to bring you food?

62
00:05:32,985 --> 00:05:34,465
I'm not hungry yet.

63
00:05:34,545 --> 00:05:37,305
Remember to eat. And did you
take the vitamins I sent you?

64
00:05:39,065 --> 00:05:40,705
<i>You need to take them, honey.</i>

65
00:05:40,785 --> 00:05:41,905
Okay, Mom.

66
00:05:42,665 --> 00:05:43,985
I should get back to work now.

67
00:05:44,585 --> 00:05:46,665
I care about you, honey.

68
00:05:47,185 --> 00:05:48,265
I know.

69
00:06:49,225 --> 00:06:50,345
Mom.

70
00:06:52,025 --> 00:06:53,345
Oh, Runch.

71
00:06:53,425 --> 00:06:54,545
You're home.

72
00:06:54,625 --> 00:06:57,545
I fell asleep for a bit.

73
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:58,745
Mom…

74
00:06:58,825 --> 00:07:00,865
Why didn't you go to bed in your room?

75
00:07:00,945 --> 00:07:02,025
Why'd you wait for me?

76
00:07:03,225 --> 00:07:05,065
I was worried about you.

77
00:07:05,145 --> 00:07:07,065
I called, but you wouldn't answer.

78
00:07:07,145 --> 00:07:09,585
I got anxious, so I sat here and waited

79
00:07:09,665 --> 00:07:11,745
so that I'd see you when you got home.

80
00:07:12,785 --> 00:07:14,145
You know,

81
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:17,025
you don't have to call me
all the time, Mom.

82
00:07:17,105 --> 00:07:18,905
I have work to do.

83
00:07:18,985 --> 00:07:20,825
Sometimes I really can't
answer your calls.

84
00:07:21,945 --> 00:07:24,865
I understand.
I didn't mean to disturb you.

85
00:07:24,945 --> 00:07:26,265
I'm just happy

86
00:07:26,345 --> 00:07:28,825
to be alone together with you like this.

87
00:07:30,385 --> 00:07:31,665
Whatever you do,

88
00:07:31,745 --> 00:07:35,145
wherever you are, or whether you're tired,
I want to know it all.

89
00:07:35,225 --> 00:07:37,025
And I care about you.

90
00:07:37,105 --> 00:07:37,945
Plus,

91
00:07:38,025 --> 00:07:41,025
it's been a while since we had
our mother-daughter bonding time.

92
00:07:41,105 --> 00:07:43,025
Since you got married,

93
00:07:43,745 --> 00:07:46,185
this is the first time
you've been this close to me.

94
00:07:49,505 --> 00:07:51,985
I didn't mean to stay away from you.

95
00:07:53,905 --> 00:07:55,385
I know.

96
00:07:55,465 --> 00:07:57,105
I'm not upset.

97
00:07:58,185 --> 00:08:00,105
I just missed you.

98
00:08:02,785 --> 00:08:04,185
You should go to bed.

99
00:08:06,985 --> 00:08:08,065
I know.

100
00:08:08,865 --> 00:08:10,505
So should you, Mom.

101
00:08:11,625 --> 00:08:13,385
-Sure.
-Let's both go to bed.

102
00:08:35,904 --> 00:08:36,825
My ring!

103
00:08:49,105 --> 00:08:50,185
Hello, Mom.

104
00:08:51,425 --> 00:08:52,665
Yes, honey?

105
00:08:53,745 --> 00:08:56,745
Could you check in the bathroom for me?

106
00:08:56,825 --> 00:09:00,425
I remember taking off my ring
and putting it by the sink.

107
00:09:00,505 --> 00:09:02,265
I forgot to wear it today.

108
00:09:06,585 --> 00:09:09,345
I checked. I didn't see a ring.

109
00:09:09,425 --> 00:09:10,545
You didn't?

110
00:09:12,305 --> 00:09:13,985
Are you sure?

111
00:09:14,065 --> 00:09:17,265
I could swear
I put it by the sink, though.

112
00:09:17,825 --> 00:09:20,105
I'm very sure. I looked all over.

113
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:21,825
There was no ring.

114
00:09:21,905 --> 00:09:23,145
How strange.

115
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:27,945
But I swear I left it by the sink.

116
00:09:28,705 --> 00:09:30,145
<i>Don't worry, honey.</i>

117
00:09:30,225 --> 00:09:32,625
Maybe you put it somewhere else.

118
00:09:32,705 --> 00:09:34,305
I'll help you find it.

119
00:09:34,385 --> 00:09:37,145
I'll search all over the place again.

120
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:40,785
If I find it,
I'll let you know right away.

121
00:10:10,945 --> 00:10:12,145
Where on earth is it?

122
00:10:25,185 --> 00:10:26,185
It's not here.

123
00:10:35,705 --> 00:10:38,425
What? The bag's replaced?

124
00:10:50,385 --> 00:10:51,785
Runch.

125
00:10:51,865 --> 00:10:54,185
Runch, where are you going?

126
00:10:54,265 --> 00:10:55,225
Runch!

127
00:11:20,185 --> 00:11:21,465
Runch!

128
00:11:21,545 --> 00:11:23,385
What are you doing?

129
00:11:23,465 --> 00:11:25,305
I'm looking for my ring.

130
00:11:25,385 --> 00:11:26,785
I told you,

131
00:11:26,865 --> 00:11:28,705
I didn't find a ring in the bathroom.

132
00:11:28,785 --> 00:11:30,305
You don't believe me?

133
00:11:30,385 --> 00:11:32,025
I distinctly remember

134
00:11:32,105 --> 00:11:34,585
putting it by the sink, Mom.

135
00:11:36,025 --> 00:11:38,305
Hey, will you stop it!

136
00:11:38,385 --> 00:11:40,425
Stop looking already! It's dirty!

137
00:11:44,985 --> 00:11:47,105
It's just a ring. What's the big deal?

138
00:11:52,025 --> 00:11:53,865
It's not just a ring.

139
00:11:55,505 --> 00:11:57,985
It's my wedding ring with Neen.

140
00:11:59,025 --> 00:12:00,905
It means a lot to me.

141
00:12:01,465 --> 00:12:03,465
I have to find it, no matter what.

142
00:12:05,425 --> 00:12:08,505
If it's not here, that means it's gone.

143
00:12:13,825 --> 00:12:15,265
What do you mean by that?

144
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:17,065
What I mean is

145
00:12:17,145 --> 00:12:19,105
some things shouldn't be kept

146
00:12:19,185 --> 00:12:21,345
if it pains everyone in the house.

147
00:12:21,945 --> 00:12:23,545
Why would you say that?

148
00:12:24,145 --> 00:12:25,185
Don't tell me…

149
00:12:30,185 --> 00:12:32,385
you threw away my ring.

150
00:12:34,745 --> 00:12:37,905
Well, it was right in front of me.

151
00:12:37,985 --> 00:12:40,185
And it made me feel uncomfortable.

152
00:12:40,785 --> 00:12:42,265
I'm asking you,

153
00:12:42,865 --> 00:12:45,425
you threw away my ring, didn't you?

154
00:12:52,345 --> 00:12:54,225
Where did you throw it away to?

155
00:12:56,545 --> 00:12:58,385
Uh, Runch--

156
00:12:58,465 --> 00:12:59,465
Answer me!

157
00:13:00,065 --> 00:13:01,065
Answer me, Mom!

158
00:13:01,145 --> 00:13:03,945
Runch, that hurts! Let me go, will you?

159
00:13:04,865 --> 00:13:06,705
So that ring matters more than me?

160
00:13:08,145 --> 00:13:09,745
Where is the ring, Mom?

161
00:14:16,145 --> 00:14:18,865
<i>Mothers will do anything,</i>

162
00:14:18,945 --> 00:14:22,225
<i>especially one</i>
<i>who's as protective as yours.</i>

163
00:14:22,305 --> 00:14:25,465
<i>She'd do it just so she wouldn't</i>
<i>lose you to someone else.</i>

164
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:29,105
<i>I think you fell for your mother's trick.</i>

165
00:14:33,705 --> 00:14:34,665
Mom.

166
00:14:37,505 --> 00:14:38,905
Please go home.

167
00:14:40,625 --> 00:14:42,185
Are you mad at me?

168
00:14:43,985 --> 00:14:45,145
I'm not.

169
00:14:46,145 --> 00:14:48,185
But you're crossing the line.

170
00:14:49,865 --> 00:14:51,985
Runch, I'm sorry.

171
00:14:52,065 --> 00:14:53,465
I didn't think it through

172
00:14:53,545 --> 00:14:55,345
What I did was wrong.

173
00:14:55,425 --> 00:14:56,705
Please don't kick me out.

174
00:14:56,785 --> 00:14:58,345
I have no one else to turn to.

175
00:15:01,065 --> 00:15:02,305
I want to stay with you.

176
00:15:02,385 --> 00:15:03,945
That's all I ask.

177
00:15:58,585 --> 00:16:00,585
Runch! No!

178
00:16:04,345 --> 00:16:05,545
It's me, it's me!

179
00:16:05,625 --> 00:16:08,025
Why were you following me?

180
00:16:08,105 --> 00:16:09,625
You scared me!

181
00:16:10,305 --> 00:16:12,225
My eyes are burning.

182
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:15,505
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to. It's just…

183
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:18,545
I didn't want you to walk away,

184
00:16:18,625 --> 00:16:21,225
so I followed you quietly.

185
00:16:21,305 --> 00:16:23,705
I didn't think you'd spray me
right in the face.

186
00:16:28,625 --> 00:16:30,305
I'm sorry for scaring you.

187
00:16:33,305 --> 00:16:34,745
But actually,

188
00:16:36,185 --> 00:16:38,585
I need your help with something.

189
00:16:38,665 --> 00:16:41,025
What do you need my help for?

190
00:16:42,465 --> 00:16:45,025
I want us to team up

191
00:16:45,105 --> 00:16:48,225
and get my mom to show her true colors.

192
00:16:49,465 --> 00:16:51,105
Am I hearing this right?

193
00:16:52,105 --> 00:16:53,465
Yes.

194
00:16:53,545 --> 00:16:55,345
You heard me right.

195
00:16:58,785 --> 00:17:00,025
But I probably

196
00:17:00,705 --> 00:17:02,545
can't handle this alone.

197
00:17:04,424 --> 00:17:06,585
If you want my mom to go home,

198
00:17:06,665 --> 00:17:08,224
we have to work together.

199
00:17:36,105 --> 00:17:37,305
What are you doing?

200
00:17:39,785 --> 00:17:41,985
Mom, you're back!

201
00:17:44,505 --> 00:17:46,905
Did you miss me, Mom?

202
00:17:48,105 --> 00:17:48,945
You're speechless.

203
00:17:49,025 --> 00:17:50,625
That means you did miss me.

204
00:17:50,705 --> 00:17:53,945
Mom, I'm back.

205
00:17:54,025 --> 00:17:55,545
I've come back to stay here,

206
00:17:55,625 --> 00:17:57,625
and I'm not going anywhere this time.

207
00:17:57,705 --> 00:18:00,545
I'll make sure you see my face every day.

208
00:18:00,625 --> 00:18:02,425
-But--
-Let's get along

209
00:18:02,505 --> 00:18:05,185
so Runch can rest easy, Mom.

210
00:18:05,265 --> 00:18:08,345
From now on, I will listen to you.

211
00:18:08,425 --> 00:18:10,985
I'll never ever go against you.

212
00:18:12,625 --> 00:18:14,425
I love you, Mom.

213
00:18:15,105 --> 00:18:17,305
I love you so much.

214
00:18:19,825 --> 00:18:21,985
Did you miss me, Mom?

215
00:18:22,065 --> 00:18:24,745
Gosh, I missed you so bad.

216
00:18:24,825 --> 00:18:27,825
I promise I won't leave you again, Mom.

217
00:18:40,825 --> 00:18:41,945
That brat!

218
00:18:42,025 --> 00:18:44,345
What do I need to do to get rid of you?

219
00:18:44,425 --> 00:18:46,305
What should I do now?

220
00:19:08,225 --> 00:19:09,185
<i>Would you all like</i>

221
00:19:09,265 --> 00:19:11,785
<i>to join us for dinner</i>
<i>at my daughter's tomorrow?</i>

222
00:19:24,545 --> 00:19:25,665
Thank you.

223
00:19:42,265 --> 00:19:43,425
I was thinking

224
00:19:43,505 --> 00:19:46,265
I'd invite my friends
to join us for dinner here today.

225
00:19:46,345 --> 00:19:48,505
Could you take care of it, Neen?

226
00:19:49,505 --> 00:19:51,585
I want a full course meal,

227
00:19:51,665 --> 00:19:54,385
and I want you
in charge of the whole meal.

228
00:19:55,905 --> 00:19:56,905
This evening?

229
00:19:58,785 --> 00:20:00,825
I'm not sure if I can prepare it in time.

230
00:20:00,905 --> 00:20:02,705
There's not nearly enough time.

231
00:20:04,225 --> 00:20:05,545
You'll have to figure it out.

232
00:20:05,625 --> 00:20:07,185
I already invited them.

233
00:20:17,745 --> 00:20:18,825
Neen,

234
00:20:19,545 --> 00:20:21,465
please do this for my mom.

235
00:20:22,425 --> 00:20:24,465
Don't disappoint her.

236
00:20:30,465 --> 00:20:31,305
Okay.

237
00:20:48,585 --> 00:20:50,105
Neen,

238
00:20:50,705 --> 00:20:52,705
you've been on your phone all day.

239
00:20:52,785 --> 00:20:55,465
You didn't get the place ready
or anything.

240
00:20:57,025 --> 00:20:58,345
Yes, Mom.

241
00:20:59,385 --> 00:21:01,785
So will you finish everything in time?

242
00:21:03,825 --> 00:21:05,985
I'm not sure.

243
00:21:07,025 --> 00:21:09,345
Well, what if you don't?

244
00:21:09,425 --> 00:21:11,505
You'll embarrass me.

245
00:21:13,345 --> 00:21:15,465
I'm really sorry, Mom.

246
00:21:15,545 --> 00:21:17,145
I'll try my best.

247
00:21:18,425 --> 00:21:19,945
You'd better hurry up, then.

248
00:21:20,025 --> 00:21:22,065
I don't want it to turn out bad.

249
00:21:22,945 --> 00:21:24,305
Sure, Mom.

250
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:50,385
You can come out now.

251
00:21:54,905 --> 00:21:58,265
Girls, I'm sorry
on behalf of my daughter-in-law.

252
00:21:58,345 --> 00:22:01,185
She couldn't get everything ready in time.

253
00:22:03,345 --> 00:22:04,665
It's just how rich kids are.

254
00:22:04,745 --> 00:22:05,825
Normally,

255
00:22:05,905 --> 00:22:08,105
her maid does everything for her,

256
00:22:08,185 --> 00:22:10,985
so when I leave her in charge,
she can't do it.

257
00:22:11,065 --> 00:22:13,065
Please don't get mad at her.

258
00:22:26,945 --> 00:22:28,025
You brat.

259
00:22:28,105 --> 00:22:29,945
This time, I'll win.

260
00:22:36,825 --> 00:22:38,585
The appetizer's good, isn't it?

261
00:22:38,665 --> 00:22:40,825
-Oh, yes, it is!
-Wait until you try the entrée.

262
00:22:40,905 --> 00:22:42,225
It's so good.

263
00:22:42,305 --> 00:22:44,265
-Really?
-Of course!

264
00:22:44,785 --> 00:22:45,865
I can't wait.

265
00:22:45,945 --> 00:22:47,545
I hope you all like it.

266
00:22:47,625 --> 00:22:49,345
The presentation's so mouth-watering.

267
00:22:49,425 --> 00:22:51,425
-True.
-Thank you so much.

268
00:22:51,505 --> 00:22:52,985
Can't wait to eat it.

269
00:22:53,065 --> 00:22:55,185
The food's so good, isn't it?

270
00:22:55,265 --> 00:22:57,385
Yeah. All the dishes look so good.

271
00:23:00,065 --> 00:23:01,225
Oh, Ging!

272
00:23:01,305 --> 00:23:02,465
Come join us!

273
00:23:03,185 --> 00:23:04,625
Mom.

274
00:23:04,705 --> 00:23:06,585
-Come on.
-Come sit with us.

275
00:23:06,665 --> 00:23:09,105
-It looks so good, doesn't it?
-Yeah.

276
00:23:09,185 --> 00:23:10,385
Oh, I can't wait.

277
00:23:12,145 --> 00:23:14,825
You know, Ging,
I've got to hand it to them.

278
00:23:14,905 --> 00:23:16,905
Neen and Runch are so sweet.

279
00:23:16,985 --> 00:23:18,625
They really took great care of us.

280
00:23:18,705 --> 00:23:20,305
Yeah.

281
00:23:20,385 --> 00:23:21,785
She's so polite and caring.

282
00:23:21,865 --> 00:23:24,305
And everything looks well-prepared.

283
00:23:24,385 --> 00:23:25,865
Mom,

284
00:23:25,945 --> 00:23:28,465
Neen's prepared
a fine dining meal for you.

285
00:23:28,545 --> 00:23:30,985
It's from a famous restaurant in Bangkok.

286
00:23:31,065 --> 00:23:34,705
Luckily, my parents love this restaurant,

287
00:23:34,785 --> 00:23:37,265
so they sent their chefs over just for us.

288
00:23:37,345 --> 00:23:39,905
Normally, they don't do off-site catering.

289
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:41,785
-Wow!
-Wow!

290
00:23:41,865 --> 00:23:43,785
Your daughter-in-law sure has connections.

291
00:23:43,865 --> 00:23:45,865
Oh, come on.

292
00:23:45,945 --> 00:23:47,625
She's really something.

293
00:23:47,705 --> 00:23:49,705
She's both talented and sophisticated.

294
00:23:49,785 --> 00:23:51,065
That's right.

295
00:23:51,585 --> 00:23:54,825
Ging, can you host a party
like this again someday?

296
00:23:54,905 --> 00:23:57,625
We'll come, no matter how far away we are.

297
00:23:57,705 --> 00:23:59,745
That's right! I loved it.

298
00:23:59,825 --> 00:24:03,265
I was really impressed today.

299
00:24:03,345 --> 00:24:05,745
Let's do this again.
I'm so happy to have you over.

300
00:24:05,825 --> 00:24:07,785
I'll invite you again someday.

301
00:24:07,865 --> 00:24:09,825
-Sure.
-Sounds good.

302
00:24:09,905 --> 00:24:12,385
See, we're both full and happy.

303
00:24:13,385 --> 00:24:16,305
-Thank you for coming.
-Aw.

304
00:24:16,385 --> 00:24:18,505
-Let's meet again soon.
-Sure.

305
00:24:18,585 --> 00:24:20,385
-We'll get going now.
-Okay.

306
00:24:20,465 --> 00:24:21,305
Drive safe.

307
00:24:21,385 --> 00:24:22,825
-Okay.
-If you'll excuse me.

308
00:24:22,905 --> 00:24:23,865
-Sure.
-We'll come again.

309
00:24:23,945 --> 00:24:25,305
-See you, Ging.
-Take care.

310
00:24:25,385 --> 00:24:26,545
Bye.

311
00:24:28,545 --> 00:24:30,385
Good job, Neen.

312
00:24:30,465 --> 00:24:32,625
I'm proud of you.

313
00:24:33,465 --> 00:24:34,625
So where's my reward?

314
00:24:35,225 --> 00:24:36,825
I'll give you one tonight.

315
00:24:36,905 --> 00:24:38,545
Hey, can't you see

316
00:24:39,145 --> 00:24:40,905
your mother's standing here?

317
00:24:45,585 --> 00:24:48,345
Anyway, I need to use the bathroom.

318
00:25:01,145 --> 00:25:03,545
You did it to embarrass me, didn't you?

319
00:25:05,385 --> 00:25:07,705
That was never my idea, Mom.

320
00:25:07,785 --> 00:25:09,785
I just want what's best for you--

321
00:25:09,865 --> 00:25:12,025
Drop the act already.

322
00:25:15,185 --> 00:25:18,305
I really doubt
someone like you could change.

323
00:25:22,305 --> 00:25:23,225
Why are you laughing?

324
00:25:25,305 --> 00:25:27,985
Couldn't keep up the act,
so you finally snapped?

325
00:25:28,065 --> 00:25:30,265
This was your plan, wasn't it?

326
00:25:30,345 --> 00:25:32,665
What are you talking about?

327
00:25:32,745 --> 00:25:34,185
I'm an innocent girl.

328
00:25:34,265 --> 00:25:36,105
I'd never scheme against you.

329
00:25:36,185 --> 00:25:37,305
You're so full of it!

330
00:25:37,945 --> 00:25:39,945
You're just a rude little brat.

331
00:25:40,625 --> 00:25:41,905
You think you're smart?

332
00:25:41,985 --> 00:25:43,465
Don't think I can't see through you.

333
00:25:46,425 --> 00:25:49,505
I'll make Runch hate you so much

334
00:25:49,585 --> 00:25:51,865
that she'll never want
to see your face again.

335
00:25:57,705 --> 00:25:59,985
-Help me, Runch! Help!
-You're crazy!

336
00:26:00,065 --> 00:26:01,825
No! Runch!

337
00:26:02,665 --> 00:26:05,425
-Runch! Runch!
-Crazy bitch! Let go!

338
00:26:05,505 --> 00:26:07,025
-Help me, Runch!
-You're crazy!

339
00:26:07,105 --> 00:26:09,705
Help me! Help!

340
00:26:09,785 --> 00:26:12,905
Runch! Runch! Runch!

341
00:26:12,985 --> 00:26:14,505
-Runch, help!
-Enough.

342
00:26:14,585 --> 00:26:15,985
Stop it!

343
00:26:16,065 --> 00:26:17,425
-Stop it!
-Runch!

344
00:26:19,705 --> 00:26:20,545
Runch,

345
00:26:20,625 --> 00:26:23,385
Neen hurt me, Runch.

346
00:26:24,145 --> 00:26:25,385
Crazy bitch!

347
00:26:25,465 --> 00:26:26,585
That's enough, Mom.

348
00:26:29,465 --> 00:26:31,865
I'm calling Dad so he can take you home.

349
00:26:32,505 --> 00:26:33,625
Why?

350
00:26:35,145 --> 00:26:36,265
Watch this.

351
00:26:38,825 --> 00:26:41,785
<i>I'll make Runch hate you so much</i>

352
00:26:41,865 --> 00:26:44,225
<i>that she'll never want</i>
<i>to see your face again.</i>

353
00:26:49,705 --> 00:26:51,545
<i>Help me, Runch!</i>

354
00:26:52,665 --> 00:26:54,385
-You installed a security camera…
<i>-You're crazy!</i>

355
00:26:54,465 --> 00:26:56,265
-…to spy on me?
<i>-Help me! Help!</i>

356
00:26:57,065 --> 00:26:58,305
Yes.

357
00:26:58,385 --> 00:27:00,345
I did it the day you threw away my ring.

358
00:27:08,425 --> 00:27:09,985
Please let me explain, Runch.

359
00:27:10,065 --> 00:27:11,145
-No.
-Please?

360
00:27:12,785 --> 00:27:14,225
I saw everything.

361
00:27:14,305 --> 00:27:16,185
I saw what you did.

362
00:27:17,385 --> 00:27:20,145
I can't let you stay here anymore.

363
00:27:26,585 --> 00:27:28,825
You planned this, didn't you, Peeracha?

364
00:27:28,905 --> 00:27:30,625
Didn't you, Peeracha?

365
00:27:30,705 --> 00:27:32,305
That's enough. Mom!

366
00:27:32,385 --> 00:27:33,465
Stop it!

367
00:27:35,825 --> 00:27:37,425
Don't you lay a finger on Neen.

368
00:27:37,505 --> 00:27:38,985
Don't hurt her.

369
00:27:40,185 --> 00:27:42,585
I did it all by myself.

370
00:27:48,225 --> 00:27:49,305
Runch…

371
00:27:52,505 --> 00:27:53,985
You should pack your things.

372
00:27:55,505 --> 00:27:57,825
I'm calling Dad so he can take you home.

373
00:28:03,025 --> 00:28:04,545
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

374
00:28:37,665 --> 00:28:39,185
Your mom's gone home already?

375
00:28:54,345 --> 00:28:56,865
I know it must be difficult for you.

376
00:28:59,145 --> 00:29:02,265
If you want to talk or vent,

377
00:29:02,345 --> 00:29:04,505
I'm always here to listen.

378
00:29:22,465 --> 00:29:24,265
Getting to hug you

379
00:29:25,745 --> 00:29:27,785
and having some peace and quiet

380
00:29:29,225 --> 00:29:30,865
is enough to cheer me up.

381
00:29:34,625 --> 00:29:35,985
Then I'll hug you tighter.

382
00:29:54,585 --> 00:29:58,145
I think we've been
too stressed out lately.

383
00:30:00,225 --> 00:30:02,185
Can you take me on a trip?

384
00:30:07,745 --> 00:30:11,425
I want to be with you like this all day
and just do nothing.

385
00:30:13,625 --> 00:30:16,385
Won't you get bored if we do this all day?

386
00:30:17,185 --> 00:30:18,505
Of course I won't.

387
00:30:18,585 --> 00:30:21,385
Just seeing your face makes me happy.

388
00:30:22,225 --> 00:30:23,665
Me too.

389
00:30:59,145 --> 00:31:00,425
What are you doing?

390
00:31:01,945 --> 00:31:02,945
I'm building a house.

391
00:31:03,585 --> 00:31:05,585
A house just for the two of us.

392
00:31:20,065 --> 00:31:22,505
It's all gone!

393
00:31:25,905 --> 00:31:27,985
That's alright.

394
00:31:28,065 --> 00:31:29,345
We can build a new one.

395
00:31:30,065 --> 00:31:32,505
This time, I'll help you build it.

396
00:31:36,705 --> 00:31:37,825
Fine.

397
00:31:40,785 --> 00:31:41,825
Come on.

398
00:32:08,865 --> 00:32:09,985
Hello.

399
00:32:12,985 --> 00:32:16,065
Yes, I'm Gingkamol, Runchlaphat's mother.

400
00:32:19,665 --> 00:32:20,785
A show?

401
00:32:20,865 --> 00:32:22,145
A show, you say?

402
00:32:30,425 --> 00:32:31,625
You're almost there.

403
00:32:31,705 --> 00:32:33,745
Just a little longer.

404
00:32:33,825 --> 00:32:37,785
In five, four, three, one.

405
00:32:37,865 --> 00:32:38,905
Here we are.

406
00:32:39,745 --> 00:32:40,745
Are you ready?

407
00:32:40,825 --> 00:32:41,745
Yes.

408
00:32:50,745 --> 00:32:52,505
‎Ta-da!

409
00:32:53,865 --> 00:32:55,465
And this is

410
00:32:55,545 --> 00:32:58,305
where we're staying tonight.

411
00:32:58,385 --> 00:33:00,385
-Yay!
-Yay!

412
00:33:00,465 --> 00:33:02,585
You're the sweetest!

413
00:33:02,665 --> 00:33:04,105
-You like it?
-Thank you.

414
00:33:04,185 --> 00:33:06,345
-Do you like it?
-I love it.

415
00:33:07,625 --> 00:33:08,625
Wow.

416
00:33:21,905 --> 00:33:22,985
Are you hungry?

417
00:33:23,705 --> 00:33:25,065
Hold tight a little longer.

418
00:33:25,145 --> 00:33:26,385
It's almost ready.

419
00:33:28,465 --> 00:33:30,585
Can I help you with anything?

420
00:33:31,945 --> 00:33:33,065
No.

421
00:33:33,145 --> 00:33:34,905
Just sit tight.

422
00:33:34,985 --> 00:33:36,425
Because today,

423
00:33:36,505 --> 00:33:38,145
you're my princess.

424
00:33:39,225 --> 00:33:40,185
Yes, ma'am.

425
00:33:40,865 --> 00:33:41,745
Yes.

426
00:33:44,785 --> 00:33:47,505
Hey. Stop. Stop it.

427
00:33:48,385 --> 00:33:49,905
I told you,

428
00:33:49,985 --> 00:33:51,945
you're my princess today.

429
00:33:52,025 --> 00:33:54,625
Don't do anything by yourself.
I'll do it for you.

430
00:33:55,545 --> 00:33:56,625
Okay.

431
00:33:59,265 --> 00:34:00,225
Here it comes.

432
00:34:13,344 --> 00:34:15,105
The shrimp is so sweet.

433
00:34:16,385 --> 00:34:18,985
I bet it's because you grilled it for me.

434
00:34:20,105 --> 00:34:21,665
-Want some more?
-Yeah.

435
00:34:29,945 --> 00:34:31,824
Can you pour me another?

436
00:34:39,625 --> 00:34:41,185
Neen.

437
00:34:41,985 --> 00:34:43,465
The bottle's empty.

438
00:34:44,065 --> 00:34:46,025
Empty. Gone.

439
00:34:48,304 --> 00:34:51,185
But I want another.

440
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:53,585
You should stop.

441
00:34:55,385 --> 00:34:58,665
We're out. No, no, no. You're drunk.

442
00:35:02,745 --> 00:35:04,425
Will you still love me if I'm drunk?

443
00:35:04,505 --> 00:35:05,785
I will.

444
00:35:06,465 --> 00:35:08,505
Drunk or not, I'll love you either way.

445
00:35:10,025 --> 00:35:11,185
I'm so glad.

446
00:35:14,625 --> 00:35:15,945
-Huh?
-Then let's go.

447
00:35:16,825 --> 00:35:18,745
Wait-- Where are you going, Neen?

448
00:35:20,425 --> 00:35:22,305
Let's dance.

449
00:35:23,025 --> 00:35:24,705
But there's no music.

450
00:35:24,785 --> 00:35:26,385
We don't need a song.

451
00:35:27,065 --> 00:35:28,665
We'll dance to the song in here.

452
00:35:29,265 --> 00:35:30,745
My song?

453
00:35:30,825 --> 00:35:31,905
In here.

454
00:35:32,905 --> 00:35:34,425
Your song too?

455
00:35:42,305 --> 00:35:44,425
And then you grab my waist.

456
00:35:45,025 --> 00:35:47,705
Like so. Right.

457
00:35:47,785 --> 00:35:49,025
And right.

458
00:35:57,625 --> 00:35:58,905
We should stop.

459
00:36:00,105 --> 00:36:01,865
You're drunk, Neen.

460
00:36:02,905 --> 00:36:04,385
And if you don't stop,

461
00:36:05,945 --> 00:36:08,305
I won't be able to stop myself.

462
00:36:10,665 --> 00:36:12,505
Then don't.

463
00:36:27,705 --> 00:36:28,905
No.

464
00:36:30,105 --> 00:36:31,305
Remember,

465
00:36:31,905 --> 00:36:34,545
you're my princess tonight.

466
00:36:36,985 --> 00:36:38,785
I'll do everything for you.

467
00:37:05,505 --> 00:37:06,985
Thank you so much

468
00:37:07,065 --> 00:37:09,025
for taking the time
to be on our show today.

469
00:37:09,665 --> 00:37:10,785
It's my pleasure.

470
00:37:10,865 --> 00:37:12,825
As long as it benefits society.

471
00:37:12,905 --> 00:37:15,425
Actually, our show, <i>Real Talk With Moms</i>

472
00:37:15,505 --> 00:37:17,225
is meant to be a space

473
00:37:17,305 --> 00:37:19,305
where parents can voice
their true feelings,

474
00:37:19,905 --> 00:37:22,225
especially about sexual diversity.

475
00:37:22,305 --> 00:37:23,825
We want the public to see

476
00:37:23,905 --> 00:37:26,865
that not every family
can easily accept it.

477
00:37:26,945 --> 00:37:28,785
But trying to understand it

478
00:37:28,865 --> 00:37:30,945
is already an important first step.

479
00:37:31,665 --> 00:37:33,025
I think so too.

480
00:37:33,105 --> 00:37:35,785
Matters like this aren't easy for mothers.

481
00:37:36,385 --> 00:37:38,425
That's right. We wanted to invite you

482
00:37:38,505 --> 00:37:40,905
because you're
one of the mothers who accepted

483
00:37:40,985 --> 00:37:42,665
your daughter's same-sex marriage,

484
00:37:42,745 --> 00:37:45,145
which not everyone can do.

485
00:37:47,465 --> 00:37:49,745
I may not understand it all,

486
00:37:49,825 --> 00:37:52,625
but I love my daughter.
And that should be enough.

487
00:37:52,705 --> 00:37:55,305
That's exactly the idea
we're trying to convey.

488
00:37:55,385 --> 00:37:56,545
The questions we ask

489
00:37:56,625 --> 00:37:58,345
aren't intended to attack anyone.

490
00:37:58,425 --> 00:38:01,385
We just want to tell each story
through a mother's lens.

491
00:38:01,465 --> 00:38:04,585
What she had to go through
before she could accept the truth.

492
00:38:04,665 --> 00:38:06,865
There's nothing to worry about.

493
00:38:06,945 --> 00:38:08,585
Just say whatever you feel.

494
00:38:08,665 --> 00:38:10,065
Say it from your heart.

495
00:38:10,145 --> 00:38:11,505
We believe the viewers

496
00:38:11,585 --> 00:38:14,025
will see that you only want
what's best for your daughter.

497
00:38:14,905 --> 00:38:17,505
Then, I'll say how I really feel.

498
00:38:17,585 --> 00:38:19,345
-Sure.
-So everyone

499
00:38:19,425 --> 00:38:21,105
will understand a mother's love.

500
00:38:21,705 --> 00:38:22,705
Yes.

501
00:38:24,825 --> 00:38:27,145
Ma'am, we'll start in five minutes.

502
00:38:27,225 --> 00:38:28,225
Okay.

503
00:38:37,265 --> 00:38:40,705
Lately, people have been talking
about your dear daughter's relationship.

504
00:38:40,785 --> 00:38:42,225
How do you feel about this?

505
00:38:43,025 --> 00:38:44,825
I, um…

506
00:38:45,425 --> 00:38:46,825
I do admit

507
00:38:46,905 --> 00:38:49,025
that it's not something I expected.

508
00:38:49,585 --> 00:38:50,945
But in the end,

509
00:38:51,025 --> 00:38:53,705
no matter what path you choose in life,

510
00:38:53,785 --> 00:38:55,985
I'll always love you just the same, honey.

511
00:38:56,065 --> 00:38:57,225
I'm just…

512
00:38:57,905 --> 00:38:58,985
worried about you.

513
00:38:59,065 --> 00:39:00,705
Many people see

514
00:39:00,785 --> 00:39:02,265
your daughter's love

515
00:39:02,345 --> 00:39:04,465
as the courage to be herself.

516
00:39:04,545 --> 00:39:06,065
Do you agree?

517
00:39:06,145 --> 00:39:08,785
I don't believe it's wrong to be yourself.

518
00:39:09,665 --> 00:39:10,985
But sometimes,

519
00:39:11,065 --> 00:39:12,945
the people in your life

520
00:39:13,025 --> 00:39:15,345
may fail to consider all the consequences,

521
00:39:15,425 --> 00:39:16,945
especially for your family.

522
00:39:17,025 --> 00:39:20,225
So you don't approve
of her current relationship?

523
00:39:20,305 --> 00:39:22,745
I don't want to say I don't approve it.

524
00:39:24,145 --> 00:39:26,425
I just want you to have an easy life,

525
00:39:27,065 --> 00:39:30,505
where you don't have to go
against the public opinion,

526
00:39:30,585 --> 00:39:34,065
where you don't have
to sacrifice anything for anyone's love.

527
00:39:34,665 --> 00:39:36,145
Rumor has it

528
00:39:36,225 --> 00:39:39,225
that you and Ms. Peeracha
fight quite often.

529
00:39:39,305 --> 00:39:40,385
Is that true?

530
00:39:40,945 --> 00:39:42,985
I've never had a fight with anyone.

531
00:39:44,025 --> 00:39:45,945
I'm just straightforward.

532
00:39:46,465 --> 00:39:47,945
And I just

533
00:39:48,025 --> 00:39:50,985
want to protect my daughter, is all.

534
00:39:51,585 --> 00:39:53,065
If one day,

535
00:39:53,145 --> 00:39:55,025
your daughter has to choose between

536
00:39:55,105 --> 00:39:56,625
family and love,

537
00:39:56,705 --> 00:39:58,385
what do you want her to choose?

538
00:40:11,345 --> 00:40:13,345
I don't want her to have to choose.

539
00:40:20,225 --> 00:40:21,745
But if love

540
00:40:23,425 --> 00:40:25,585
makes you turn against your family,

541
00:40:27,865 --> 00:40:29,785
I have no choice but to leave you alone…

542
00:40:32,185 --> 00:40:33,745
and hope that one day

543
00:40:36,305 --> 00:40:38,305
you'll understand how a mother feels.

544
00:40:43,225 --> 00:40:45,905
If Ms. Peeracha watches this show,

545
00:40:45,985 --> 00:40:47,905
do you have something to tell her?

546
00:40:55,145 --> 00:40:56,505
I was never angry

547
00:40:57,265 --> 00:40:58,825
or hateful toward anyone.

548
00:41:00,505 --> 00:41:02,385
I just want her to know that

549
00:41:03,745 --> 00:41:05,385
loving someone

550
00:41:06,945 --> 00:41:09,465
shouldn't come at the cost of breaking…

551
00:41:11,345 --> 00:41:13,065
a mother's heart.

552
00:41:33,065 --> 00:41:34,665
1 YEAR AGO

553
00:41:34,745 --> 00:41:36,745
Over the two years we've been together,

554
00:41:37,425 --> 00:41:39,145
we've been through a lot, haven't we?

555
00:41:41,345 --> 00:41:43,105
Just seeing your face

556
00:41:43,785 --> 00:41:46,825
makes me feel like
everything will get easier.

557
00:41:57,025 --> 00:41:58,785
If we ever feel tired,

558
00:42:00,505 --> 00:42:02,545
can I stay by your side just like this?

559
00:42:04,425 --> 00:42:05,585
Of course.

560
00:42:06,345 --> 00:42:07,305
No matter when,

561
00:42:07,385 --> 00:42:10,025
my arms will always be open for you.

562
00:42:10,985 --> 00:42:13,545
Then, do you promise

563
00:42:14,185 --> 00:42:16,465
that we'll always be each other's home?

564
00:42:18,265 --> 00:42:19,425
I promise.

565
00:42:20,185 --> 00:42:21,825
I won't let go now.

566
00:42:29,625 --> 00:42:30,705
Are you ready?

567
00:42:31,505 --> 00:42:32,745
-Yes.
-Yes.

568
00:42:41,345 --> 00:42:42,625
Are you ready, Ms. Peeracha?

569
00:42:42,705 --> 00:42:44,705
-Yes.
-Okay.

570
00:42:45,305 --> 00:42:48,225
What do you like about Ms. Runchlaphat?

571
00:42:52,545 --> 00:42:54,185
I'll keep it short.

572
00:42:55,985 --> 00:42:58,345
Runch is someone who makes me feel

573
00:42:59,505 --> 00:43:01,545
like I don't have to try to be anyone.

574
00:43:03,025 --> 00:43:04,945
Normally, I'm the type

575
00:43:05,025 --> 00:43:07,145
to overthink and imagine things,

576
00:43:07,225 --> 00:43:09,225
wondering if I'm good enough.

577
00:43:10,265 --> 00:43:12,905
But when I'm with her,

578
00:43:13,785 --> 00:43:15,305
she makes me feel like

579
00:43:15,905 --> 00:43:18,385
I don't have to be capable or strong,

580
00:43:18,465 --> 00:43:21,025
and I don't have to feel okay
all the time.

581
00:43:22,225 --> 00:43:25,825
As long as I'm me,
she'll always be by my side.

582
00:43:27,225 --> 00:43:29,065
Plus,

583
00:43:29,145 --> 00:43:31,225
Runch is the type of person who,

584
00:43:31,305 --> 00:43:33,625
even if the whole world was against me,

585
00:43:33,705 --> 00:43:36,265
would always be there for me

586
00:43:36,345 --> 00:43:38,665
without asking questions.

587
00:43:40,185 --> 00:43:42,825
It just feels so secure

588
00:43:42,905 --> 00:43:45,345
to have someone
who you can take a rest with,

589
00:43:45,425 --> 00:43:46,985
cry with,

590
00:43:47,065 --> 00:43:49,585
and dream of a future with.

591
00:43:51,865 --> 00:43:52,825
There.

592
00:43:52,905 --> 00:43:55,785
If you asked me what I like about her,
that would be my answer.

593
00:43:58,465 --> 00:43:59,425
Wait.

594
00:44:00,345 --> 00:44:02,225
That was so long.
That wasn't short at all.

595
00:44:02,905 --> 00:44:04,025
Was it too long?

596
00:44:07,145 --> 00:44:09,185
If it were me,
of course I'd choose my mother.

597
00:44:09,265 --> 00:44:12,825
Your words
made the whole country see it that way.

598
00:44:12,905 --> 00:44:15,505
-See what?
-That Neen's the one who took me

599
00:44:15,585 --> 00:44:16,705
away from you.

600
00:44:16,785 --> 00:44:19,425
If you choose to keep this up,

601
00:44:19,505 --> 00:44:21,225
I'll have to decide.

602
00:44:22,345 --> 00:44:23,985
Runch, Runch!

603
00:44:24,065 --> 00:44:25,985
From now on, no matter what we face,

604
00:44:26,065 --> 00:44:27,785
we won't let go of each other's hands.

605
00:44:27,865 --> 00:44:29,785
I feel so lucky

606
00:44:30,385 --> 00:44:31,945
to have you by my side.

607
00:45:18,505 --> 00:45:20,505
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya

